  "title": "Blackstone's AirTrunk seeks S$2 billion loan for Singapore",
  "lede": "AirTrunk, the Asia-Pacific data centre operator owned by Blackstone, is seeking a loan of around S$2 billion as it prepares for a potential listing in Singapore. The financing would support the company's operations and expansion ahead of what could be one of the region's largest data centre IPOs. A Singapore debut would give public-market investors rare direct exposure to APAC hyperscale infrastructure. Malaysia's Data Centre Task Force has assessed more than 40 proposals this year from companies seeking to build or expand data centers, weighing investment value against energy, water and connectivity requirements. Data center projects accounted for 44 percent of total investment into the country in the first half of 2026. Planning authorities have cleared a three-building, five-storey data centre campus on Glendenning Road in Sydney's west, with an estimated maximum electrical demand of 235MW and a project value of AUD 2.17 billion. The development is reported to be for Amazon Web Services, though the formal application lists Lehr Consultants International (Australia) as the proponent.",
